      "writtenOn": "2025-03-10T14:40:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The entirety of the body of this fuction should be inside a `#ifdef SK_PRINT_CODEC_MESSAGES` (or better an equivelent `if constexpr`). The `SK_PRINT_CODEC_MESSAGES` define is never set by the build, this is \"developer code\", which really only exists for developer builds when debugging. So Skia is currently getting here, making the call through this function pointer (which in this case is set by an external library to point at a function in an external library, see [icall documentation](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ControlFlowIntegrity.html#indirect-function-call-checking)) to set up a message, and then not doing anything with the result.",
      "revId": "8aa11efe05a0c24228068f99ad66ff63c9a167f5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
